It’s said that the moon’s gravitational pull brings an increase of social tension and disharmony. So, if you find yourself suddenly busting out in tears or feeling more anxious during the full moon, this could be why. The solution: Practice self-care during the full moon, focusing on activities that allow you to release and rebalance your emotions. The Full Moon Increases Creativity
The way the moon affects mental health isn’t all negative. In fact, the full moon is a great time to do something artistic, as the gravitational pull is believed to increase creative energies. The solution: Dance, write, journal, paint, draw, sing, craft – do it all! The Full Moon Expands and Magnifies Everything
